description:
After asyncfilemonitor-as7 and asyncfilemonitor-2vi there are four public factories (url/paths x per-event/batched), each carrying sinceWhen and latency. Adding qos (asyncfilemonitor-nav), granularity (asyncfilemonitor-9cr) and watchRoot (asyncfilemonitor-ekx) would take that to four signatures x six parameters.

Introduce:

  public struct Configuration: Sendable {
      public var sinceWhen: FSEventStreamEventId = .init(kFSEventStreamEventIdSinceNow)
      public var latency: CFTimeInterval = 0
  }
  public static func makeStream(url: URL, configuration: Configuration = .init()) throws -> ...

Four signatures, permanently: the three P3 options then become field additions rather than API changes.

Must ship IN 3.0. It moves sinceWhen: and latency: behind configuration:, so doing it later means waiting for 4.0.
